FerrionOS change to the Redox installer (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 16d39fe1f20f15fc97fa3aaa216ac7e449637d41 (security roadmap S13, lockdown):
- the fast install clones the live disk from lived's read-only view of the boot image, /scheme/disk.live/1 (base's ferrion-live-disk-view.patch), instead of mapping it from physical memory, which only drivers may open. Like the old clone it copies the image as booted, without what the live session wrote.
- it is tried when the disk.live scheme exists instead of when the bootloader's DISK_LIVE_* variables are in the environment, which a login shell does not have.
- installer_tui and installer-gui leave the disk.live scheme out of the target disks; the gui skipped a stale name, disk/live.

